# Round 188 — 2610.30538 misstates Bourin's conjecture; second-pick hunts clean

* 2610.30538 restates Bourin's conjecture (Linear Algebra Appl. 292 (1999), 139–154) without its hypothesis Z ∈ M_n⁺: the
  original asks ‖AZB‖ ≤ √2 ‖ZAB‖ for a monotone pair (A, B) and Z ≥ 0, for every symmetric norm. Our trivial
  counterexample (Z = E₂₁) refutes only the restatement. Bourin's original remains open; a numerical search follows.
* No counterexample (small cases): 2610.27640 (windows for cut-and-project sets; √2, √3, two windows), 2610.30503
  (Linearity Conjecture for blocking sets, q = 3: no minimal nontrivial small blocking set), 2610.24148 (strong sl₂
  actions versus symmetric chain decompositions: Boolean lattices B₀..B₇, chains ≤ 100), 2610.28762 (p_c < p_sc on
  regular trees, d ≤ 20), 2610.25571 (ρ(n) = 3n, n ≤ 4), 2610.31363 (quadratic probing, n ≤ 19), 2610.22970
  (polygon area ratios, n ≤ 80).
